<title>INDIA: India forex reserves ease to $26.65 bln on May 2.</title>
<headline>India forex reserves ease to $26.65 bln on May 2.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's foreign exchange reserves fell to $26.65 billon on May 2 against $26.75 billion the previous week, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said in its weekly statistical supplement on Monday.</p>
<p>	 Foreign exchange reserves (in million U.S. dollars)</p>
<p>					  May 2	 Apr 25	 May 3</p>
<p>					   1997	  1997	   1996</p>
<p>    Foreign currency assets     22,656	22,673	 17,073</p>
<p>    Gold				 3,966	 4,054	  4,520</p>
<p>    SDRs				    26	    27	     12</p>
<p>    Total			     26,648	26,754	 21,605</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
